<title>BRAZIL: Brazil NNE sugar exports 32 pct down in Sept/March.</title>
<headline>Brazil NNE sugar exports 32 pct down in Sept/March.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipments of sugar since September from Brazil's key north/northeast ports of Recife and Maceio are running around 32 percent behind last year's levels, according to port authority statistics.</p>
<p>Since the start of September 1996 to the end of March this year 1.11 million tonnes of sugar have been exported against 1.64 million tonnes in the same period the previous year.</p>
<p>A breakdown of shipments per month follows in tonnes.</p>
